                EHM/MRO  NOTES FOR THE OPERATIONS ROOM
                =====================================

                RELEASE 4.2C            09-FEB-1996


1.  THE DAILY CYCLE
    ---------------

    22:30   THE ACARS GATEWAY CLOSES THE DAY AND WRITES THE FLIGHT
            REPORT EXTRACT.
    23:00   EHMNITE.SH RUNS.  IT LOADS THE FOUR DATA SETS, SWEEPS
            THE FLEET, BUILDS THE INDUCTION PLAN, PROVISIONS IT
            AGAINST THE SPARES POOL AND PRINTS THE LISTING TO
            EHM.LIS.
    23:20   THE LISTING IS SPOOLED TO THE PRINTER IN THE OPERATIONS
            ROOM AND A COPY IS KEPT FOR FOURTEEN DAYS.
    07:30   THE DUTY CONTROLLER WORKS THE ALERT REPORT.

    IF THE JOB DOES NOT COMPLETE, THE PREVIOUS LISTING STANDS.  THE
    SYSTEM WRITES NOTHING BACK TO THE MASTERS SO A FAILED RUN CANNOT
    CORRUPT ANYTHING, IT ONLY LOSES A DAY OF TRENDING.


2.  READING THE ALERT REPORT
    ------------------------

    LEVEL   MEANING
    -----   -------------------------------------------------------
    AOG     THE ENGINE IS ALREADY DECLARED UNSERVICEABLE.  A BAY IS
            WANTED AT THE EARLIEST WEEK REGARDLESS OF ANYTHING ELSE.
    ACT     ACT NOW.  MARGIN AT OR BELOW THE RED LINE, A VIBRATION
            EXCEEDANCE, A LIFE LIMIT REACHED, OR A SHOP VISIT DATE
            ALREADY PAST.
    WTCH    WATCH.  REVIEW AT THE NEXT SWEEP.

    REASON  MEANING
    -----   -------------------------------------------------------
    M       EGT MARGIN LOW
    R       DETERIORATION RATE ABOVE THE LIMIT
    V       VIBRATION EXCEEDANCE
    O       OIL SYSTEM, TWO OR MORE LOW PRESSURE READINGS
    L       LIFE LIMITED PART CYCLES REACHED
    D       SHOP VISIT DUE INSIDE THE PLANNING WINDOW OR PAST

    AN EGT MARGIN PRINTED AS -1 MEANS NO FLIGHT REPORTS WERE HELD FOR
    THE ENGINE.  THE ENGINE IS STILL CHECKED FOR PART LIVES AND FOR
    THE SHOP VISIT DATE.

    CYCLES REMAINING OF 999999 MEANS THE MARGIN IS NOT DETERIORATING
    ON THE REPORTS HELD.  IT IS NOT A GUARANTEE, IT IS THE ABSENCE OF
    A TREND.


3.  WHEN THE PLAN IS SHORT OF BAYS
    ------------------------------

    EVERY ENGINE THAT NEEDS A SHOP VISIT APPEARS ON THE PLAN.  WHERE
    NO BAY COULD BE FOUND THE SHOP AND WEEK COLUMNS ARE BLANK AND THE
    STATUS READS NO SLOT AVAILABLE.  THE COUNT AT THE FOOT OF THE
    PLAN IS THE SHORTFALL TO PUT TO FLEET PLANNING.  DO NOT REKEY THE
    SLOT FILE TO FORCE A PLACEMENT, THE BAYS ARE REAL.


4.  READING THE SPARES PROVISIONING REPORT
    --------------------------------------

    THE PROVISIONING PASS WORKS THE INDUCTION PLAN IN PLAN ORDER AND
    DRAWS ONE UNIT OF EVERY PART NUMBER CARDED FOR THE ENGINE MARK
    AND THE WORKSCOPE OF THE LINE.  THE EARLIER LINES THEREFORE TAKE
    THE STOCK FIRST, WHICH IS HOW THE BAYS WILL BE FILLED.

    STATUS                      MEANING
    -----------------------     -----------------------------------
    SUPPORTED                   EVERY PART IS ON THE SHELF.
    SHORT, LEAD TIME RECOVERS   A PART IS OFF THE SHELF BUT IS ON
                                PURCHASE ORDER AND THE LEAD TIME
                                LANDS IT ON OR BEFORE THE INDUCTION
                                WEEK.  CHASE THE ORDER.
    SHORT AT INDUCTION WEEK     A PART WILL NOT BE THERE FOR THE
                                WEEK.  PUT THE LINE TO THE STORES
                                OFFICE AND THE DUTY PLANNER.
    NO PARTS LISTED             NO PART NUMBER IS CARDED FOR THAT
                                MARK AND WORKSCOPE.  IT IS A GAP IN
                                SPARES.DAT, NOT A CLEAR LINE.

    A LINE WITH NO BAY HAS NO INDUCTION WEEK TO WORK TO, SO A PART ON
    ORDER IS TAKEN AS RECOVERABLE FOR THAT LINE.

    THE PART SHORTFALL SUMMARY LISTS ONLY THE PART NUMBERS THAT RAN
    OUT.  A ROTABLE THAT IS SHORT IS CHASED THROUGH THE REPAIR LOOP,
    A CONSUMABLE IS BOUGHT.


5.  CHANGING THE LIMITS
    -------------------

    THE TREND LIMITS ARE COMPILED IN, IN INCLUDE/EHM.H.  THEY COME
    FROM THE MAINTENANCE MANUAL CHAPTER 72-00-00 AND MAY ONLY BE
    CHANGED ON A WRITTEN INSTRUCTION FROM POWERPLANT ENGINEERING.
    RECORD ANY CHANGE IN HISTORY AND REBUILD THE WHOLE SYSTEM, NOT
    JUST THE MODULE YOU EDITED.  THE HEADER IS INCLUDED EVERYWHERE.


6.  IF THE LISTING LOOKS WRONG
    --------------------------

    A)  CHECK THE RUN DATE ON THE PAGE HEADING.  A STALE RUN DATE
        MAKES EVERY SHOP VISIT LOOK OVERDUE.
    B)  CHECK EHM-101 AND EHM-102 IN THE LOG FOR THE RECORD COUNTS.
        A SHORT FLIGHT REPORT FILE IS THE USUAL CAUSE OF A FLEET THAT
        SUDDENLY LOOKS HEALTHY.
    C)  CHECK FOR TRUNCATION MESSAGES, EHM-911, EHM-916 AND EHM-925.
    D)  A PROVISIONING REPORT THAT IS ALL NO PARTS LISTED MEANS THE
        SPARES FILE WAS NOT FOUND.  CHECK FOR EHM-924 AND EHM-109 IN
        THE LOG.
    E)  KEEP THE LOG.  IT IS APPENDED TO, NOT OVERWRITTEN, AND IT IS
        THE ONLY RECORD OF WHAT THE OVERNIGHT JOB SAW.
